    ootOriginEmuRole: "Emulator used in every recorded validation.",
    ootOriginEmuSource: "Third-party; not distributed with the project.",
    ootOriginsNote: "The project integrates the decompilation; it does not rewrite it. The port's own adaptations live in the platform layers and the graphics engine. When a conclusion changes, the history records the correction instead of erasing the previous one.",
    ootStudiesEyebrow: "05 / ENGINEERING STUDIES",
    ootStudiesTitle: "Problem, investigation, decision, result, and limit<span class=\"heading-period\">.</span>",
    ootStudiesLead: "Each study exists because a previous conclusion was measured — and, in some cases, refuted. The history preserves the correction instead of erasing the mistake.",
    ootLabelProblem: "Problem",
    ootLabelInvestigation: "Investigation",
    ootLabelDecision: "Decision",
    ootLabelResult: "Result",
    ootLabelLimit: "Limit",
    ootLabelEvidence: "Evidence",
    ootStudyOneTitle: "The mip cost was arithmetic, not texture swapping",
    ootStudyOneProblem: "Phase 8 had folded the mip selector's arithmetic, the level choice, and the texture swap into one number. No build had priced an isolated swap.",
    ootStudyOneInvestigation: "Four builds in the same lineage: chain off, delivered chain, selector computed and discarded, and one forced swap per triangle with the same id. Two captures per build, panel md5, and counter readings.",
    ootStudyOneDecision: "Keep the chain enabled as a trade-off under evaluation, with the chain-off build declared as an alternative. The swap price was isolated at 0.45 µs.",
    ootStudyOneResult: "Arithmetic costs 15.7 ms of the chain's 16.4 ms (96%). The 662 forced swaps cost 0.3 ms and changed 0 pixels. Grouping primitives by level does not pay off.",
    ootStudyOneLimit: "One room and one angle, on emulator. The swap price includes batch breaking; the per-level cost includes cache scanning. The rasterizer is not part of s. The chain remains under evaluation: −31% grain for +16.4 ms.",
    ootStudyOneEvidence: "Captures f12a1/f12a3, f12f1, and f12e1; r and s counters on HUD lines 8 and 22. Data in OTD-030.",
    ootStudyTwoTitle: "The white room was the port, not the game",
    ootStudyTwoProblem: "The room looked colorless. The translator's comment justified the white with a false measurement: it claimed 605 of 979 vertices had blue above red and that vertex color was not color.",
    ootStudyTwoInvestigation: "Census of the room's 979 vertices and of the 359 extracted rooms, plus an A/B with a single switch: GE_VTX_SHADE 0 versus 1 in the same lineage.",
    ootStudyTwoDecision: "Use vertex color in MODULATE when there is no lighting, as the room's own list requests.",
    ootStudyTwoResult: "Zero of 979 vertices had blue above red; mean (96, 81, 59). Panel luminance fell 71% (47.5% → 13.6%) and the stone gained a gradient, for +0.5 ms and no change in FPS.",
    ootStudyTwoLimit: "The check is against what the list requests, not against an N64 reference. Only one room was seen in the emulator; the other 358 were read offline. 14.9% of triangles still need RSP lighting.",
    ootStudyTwoEvidence: "Captures f10c/f10e; counters s611 l0 o35 and an offline census of 611 MODULATE / 35 OTHER. Data in OTD-028.",
    ootStudyThreeTitle: "Two textures in a second pass",
    ootStudyThreeProblem: "The combiner that blends two textures by transparency was the translator's biggest gap. The DS cannot read the screen as a source.",
    ootStudyThreeInvestigation: "Draw the surface a second time with the second image and the effect weight, using POLY_ALPHA. Census of the 359 rooms to measure zero alpha, second-image segment, and format.",
    ootStudyThreeDecision: "Approximate the effect with a second pass over what is already drawn, without framebuffer reads. Bake as opaque when the second image has zero alpha in every texel.",
    ootStudyThreeResult: "In Bmori1_room_0, 560 pixels change with +1.3 ms. That is 35 second passes and 247 rebinds. The family has 21,041 triangles; 11.4% depended on the opaque bake.",
    ootStudyThreeLimit: "It is an alpha approximation: ENVA/255 on the RDP versus POLY_ALPHA/31 on the GE, a half-level error (~1.6%). 19.3% of triangles have a CI/IA/I second image, outside the RGBA16 path. One room and one angle.",
    ootStudyThreeEvidence: "Captures f11j/f11n and a 560 px diff; xluTris and r counters. Data in OTD-029, with the segment 2 correction recorded in OTD-030.",
    ootStudyFourTitle: "The gain was in the integer size",
    ootStudyFourProblem: "The previous phase pointed to the eye-space area formulation as the next mip chain cost cut.",
    ootStudyFourInvestigation: "Build the exact version, the mean-depth version, and the version with projected corners clamped to 750 px; compare render time, chosen levels, and panel md5.",
    ootStudyFourDecision: "Accept the 750 px per-corner clamp, which keeps the four area multiplications in 32 bits, and discard the exact eye-space formulation.",
    ootStudyFourResult: "The exact version cost 48.9 ms versus 47.7 ms for the old selector; mean depth tied. With the clamp, render fell to 46.5 ms without changing a pixel. Zero of 646 faces diverged between selectors.",
    ootStudyFourLimit: "The gain is 1.2 ms, 7% of the chain's 17.5 ms; FPS does not change. The 750 px clamp was checked in one room and three views. The remaining cost is in the per-corner projection's 64-bit multiplications.",
    ootStudyFourEvidence: "Builds f9a/f9b/f9c2/f9e; lodEyeDiv/lodEyeMax and lodClamp counters; panel md5 per angle. Data in OTD-027.",
    ootStudyFiveTitle: "The confetti was minification",
    ootStudyFiveProblem: "The first textured room appeared covered in colored speckle. The inherited hypothesis was a wrong CI palette.",
    ootStudyFiveInvestigation: "Compare the palette with the list data and measure face scale. A 4096× error in projected position caused 467 of 646 faces to fail a guard.",
    ootStudyFiveDecision: "Keep the palette and attack minification with a per-triangle mip chain, after fixing the camera ruler and the probe scale.",
    ootStudyFiveResult: "The palette was right; the GE samples one texel per pixel, with no filtering. Once the probe was fixed, the histogram became Lo 2/25/256/363. The chain cut grain by 32%, at a cost of +17.5 ms.",
    ootStudyFiveLimit: "Gain and cost were measured in one room and one angle. The mip chain remains a trade-off under evaluation; the ROOM_ANGLE sweep is still pending.",
    ootStudyFiveEvidence: "Captures bm33 (before), mf0 (phase 7), and f10e (after color); level histogram and panel md5. Data in OTD-023, OTD-024, and OTD-025.",
    ootGalleryEyebrow: "06 / GALLERY",
    ootGalleryTitle: "Real captures, with declared conditions<span class=\"heading-period\">.</span>",
    ootGalleryLead: "The images are melonDS 1.1 captures in DS mode, taken as evidence. They are not illustrative renders or fabricated gameplay. Superseded states are labeled.",
